{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,4]],"date-time":"2026-07-04T15:57:11Z","timestamp":1783180631172,"version":"3.54.6"},"reference-count":24,"publisher":"MDPI AG","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2023,12,19]],"date-time":"2023-12-19T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1702944000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["U20A0193"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["U20A0193"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["62003354"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["62003354"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Remote Sensing"],"abstract":"<jats:p>Low Earth Orbit (LEO) satellite communication systems typically achieve identity authentication through the encryption and decryption of two-way information, which requires complex key management systems. In contrast, the integration of navigation and communication (NavCom) signals provides novel opportunities for physical observation and authentication solutions due to its measurement functions. This paper introduces a novel signal authentication scheme based on twice two-way satellite time transfer (TWSTT) for LEO satellite systems. It leverages the non-mutated nature of the clock difference to ascertain the legitimacy of the signal by measuring the clock difference of signals at different instances. Unlike traditional authentication methods, this approach directly exploits the temporal and spatial characteristics of the signal, negating the necessity for intricate authorization key systems. Additionally, it adeptly tackles the challenges posed by spoofing interference. The performance analysis indicates that this scheme can achieve a high detection probability for the repeater spoofing signal in the low carrier-to-noise ratio conditions.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3390\/rs16010010","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,12,19]],"date-time":"2023-12-19T11:17:24Z","timestamp":1702984644000},"page":"10","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3390\/mdpi_crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":3,"title":["A NavCom Signal Authentication Scheme Based on Twice Two-Way Satellite Time Transfer"],"prefix":"10.3390","volume":"16","author":[{"given":"Xiaomei","family":"Tang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electronic Science, National University of Defense Technology, Changsha 410073, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1593-6912","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Sixin","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electronic Science, National University of Defense Technology, Changsha 410073, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jiyang","family":"Liu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electronic Science, National University of Defense Technology, Changsha 410073, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Feixue","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electronic Science, National University of Defense Technology, Changsha 410073, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"1968","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2023,12,19]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Ruggieri, M. (2006). Next Generation of Wired and Wireless Networks: The NavCom Integration, Kluwer Academic Publishers.","DOI":"10.1007\/s11277-006-9040-y"},{"key":"ref_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Ji, J., Liu, Y., Chen, W., Wu, D., Lu, H., and Zhang, J. (2021). A Novel Signal Design and Performance Analysis in NavCom Based on LEO Constellation. Sensors, 21.","DOI":"10.3390\/s21248235"},{"key":"ref_3","unstructured":"Yuan, M. (2022). Security Authentication Technologies for GNSS Signals, National University of Defense Technology."},{"key":"ref_4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Gamba, M., Nicola, M., and Motella, B. (2021). Computational Load Analysis of a Galileo OSNMA-Ready Receiver for ARM-Based Embedded Platforms. Sensors, 21.","DOI":"10.3390\/s21020467"},{"key":"ref_5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Gamba, M., Nicola, M., and Motella, B. (2020, January 22\u201325). GPS Chimera: A Software Profiling Analysis. Proceedings of the 33rd International Technical Meeting of the Satellite Division of the Institute of Navigation, Online.","DOI":"10.33012\/2020.17717"},{"key":"ref_6","unstructured":"Diglys, D. (2010). The Use of Characteristic Features of Wireless Cellular Networks for Transmission of GNSS Assistance and Correction Data, IEEE."},{"key":"ref_7","unstructured":"Liang, J. (2019). Investigation on Iridium STL Positioning Method, Huazhong University of Science and Technology."},{"key":"ref_8","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"163","DOI":"10.1007\/s10291-014-0368-6","article-title":"Performance evaluation of MSK and OFDM modulations for future GNSS signals","volume":"18","author":"Liu","year":"2014","journal-title":"GPS Solut."},{"key":"ref_9","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Diez, J., Castro, D., Palomo, J.M., and Tossaint, M. (2010, January 8\u201310). Integrated navigation and communication system based on OFDM. Proceedings of the 2010 5th ESA Workshop on Satellite Navigation Technologies and European Workshop on GNSS Signals and Signal Processing (NAVITEC), Noordwijk, The Netherlands.","DOI":"10.1109\/NAVITEC.2010.5707995"},{"ke